1
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,760
克拉克森：在今晚的《Top Gear》里，
CLARKSON: In tonight's Top Gear,

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,560
法国佬彻底疯掉的铁证。
evidence that the French have gone mad.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,640
德国佬彻底疯掉的铁证。
Evidence that the Germans have gone mad.

4
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:16,600
[惊呼]
而作为仅存的理智绿洲，
老奶奶们杀回来了！
[EXCLAIMS]
And, as an oasis of sanity,
the grannies are back.

5
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:18,840
[片头主题曲奏响]
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

6
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,400
但首先，瞧瞧我们的演播室！
But first, look at our set!

7
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:26,080
我们准备了靠垫，准备了鲜花，
还准备了巧克力，
We've got cushions, we've got flowers,
we've got chocolates,

8
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:28,440
我还备了口气清新剂。
I've got some breath freshener.

9
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:30,440
这是因为今晚要在
And that's because the star

10
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:33,920
廉价车环节出场的大牌明星
虽然看着像个假小子，
we have tonight in our reasonably-priced
car may look like a boy,

11
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:37,720
但他其实名叫塔拉。
[笑声]
but he is in fact called Tara.
[LAUGHTER]

12
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,760
所以我想，这说明“他”其实是个姑娘。
And that, I suppose, makes him a girl.

13
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,480
但这毕竟还是个汽车节目，
所以，来看车吧。
But this is still a car programme,
so the cars.

14
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,560
本田NSX，
可算不上什么惊天动地的成功之作。
The Honda NSX,
not a spectacular success story.

15
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,840
虽然它当年是由埃尔顿·塞纳一手调校的，
但去年他们总共才卖了……
It may well have been developed by
Ayrton Senna, but last year they sold

16
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,920
八台。所以他们给它做了个中期改款。
eight. So they've given it a facelift.

17
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:56,520
呃，反正就是换了套大灯而已，
还造出了这个Type R版本，
Well, a new set of headlamps anyway,
and produced this Type R version

18
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,040
车身更轻，悬挂也更硬。
which is lighter and stiffer.

19
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,880
眼下，他们正琢磨着
And, they're currently trying to decide

20
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,080
到底要不要
把它引进到英国来卖，
whether or not
they should sell it in Britain,

21
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:03,880
于是他们给我们打了个电话，说道：
so they rang us up and they said,

22
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:08,360
“你们那位斯提格，要是我从日本
运一台过去，
"Your Stig, if we ship
one of these over from Japan,

23
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:12,400
“他能不能开上赛道，在车里来段说唱（rap）？”
"could he take it out on your track
and do a rap in it?"

24
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:16,760
我们说不行，他更喜欢抒情轻音乐……
噢，是跑一圈（lap）啊！
We said no, he prefers easy listening...
Oh, a lap!

25
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:21,600
噢，对，跑圈！没问题，乐意效劳。
Oh, right, a lap! Yes, happy to oblige.

26
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:24,640
克拉克森：我非常怀疑它能不能打破
韦斯特菲尔德创下的纪录，
CLARKSON: I doubt very much it'll break
the record set by the Westfield,

27
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,240
1分23秒。
one minute 23 seconds.

28
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:29,720
它或许很轻，但也没轻到那种地步。
It may be light but it's not that light.

29
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,520
发动机里的气门结构或许挺聪明，
And the engine may have clever valves,

30
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:34,600
但说到底也还是一台3.2升V6。
but it's still only a 3.2-litre V6.

31
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:38,500
当然了，瞧瞧这天气！
又是一如既往的糟糕透顶。
And, of course, look at that weather!
That's atrocious once again.

32
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:44,300
噢，斯提格！这周听的是拉尔夫·麦克泰尔的
《伦敦街头》。
Oh, Stig! Ralph McTell this week,
Streets of London.

33
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:49,840
这车身甩得可真够横的。
噢，他差点直接冲出赛道了！
And that's very sideways.
Oh, and he's nearly off the track there!

34
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:52,120
这台车唯一
还能有一线生机的可能，
The only way
this car really stands a chance

35
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:55,360
就是它的底盘真是什么
逆天的旷世神作。
is if its chassis is
some kind of wonder thing.

36
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:58,040
哇哦，瞧瞧这个。
Ooh, and look at that.

37
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:00,760
不过这手控车真漂亮，斯提格。
That's a nice piece of driving
though, Stig.

38
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:02,780
♪ 隔着茶杯的边缘 ♪
♪ 打量着这个世界 ♪
♪ Looking at the world ♪
♪ Over the rim of his teacup ♪

39
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:06,720
老款NSX大多数时候都挑不出毛病，
但一逼到极限边缘，
The old NSX was very good most of the time,
but at the minute,

40
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:11,200
它的容错率就跟把亚历克·吉尼斯关进禁闭箱的看守一样——冷酷无情。
it was as forgiving as that guard who put
Alec Guinness in a box.

41
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,360
这台表现怎么样？
What's this one like?

42
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:16,880
重刹入弯，
一把切进去……他在跟车较劲！
Very heavy braking,
turns in... he's fighting!

43
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:21,120
好，还剩最后一个弯，要破的目标是1分23秒。
Right, one corner to go, 1:23 to beat.

44
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,320
横着漂过来了。成绩是1分33秒。
Sideways. And it's 1:33.

45
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:26,200
太神了。
That is fantastic.

46
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:30,360
1分33秒，这就意味着，呃，它比法拉利575
还要快整整两秒。
1:33, That makes it uh, two seconds faster
than a Ferrari 575.

47
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,400
而且比阿斯顿·马丁Vanquish还要快三秒。
简直不可思议。
And three seconds faster than the
Aston Martin Vanquish. That's fabulous.

48
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:36,280
克拉克森：别忘了，
这还是在干地上的综合换算。
- 噢。
CLARKSON: And, bear in mind,
you know, the dry track and everything.
- Oh.

49
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,520
要是换成干地，再扣掉四秒，
那这车可就真快得飞起了。
Take four seconds off for a dry track,
that's a quick car.

50
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:42,480
我是说，刚才那赛道可是湿得一塌糊涂，
斯提格也确实是拼了老命了。
I mean, that was a very wet track
and The Stig really was trying.

51
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,360
天呐！
- 克拉克森：嗷！
Oh, my word!
- CLARKSON: Ooh!

52
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:50,280
噢！[轻笑]
他刚才离那一堆轮胎可真够近的。
Oh! [CHUCKLES]
He was a bit close to those tyres.

53
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,400
哈蒙德：差点就赶上
阿斯顿·马丁Vanquish撞车那出惨剧了。
HAMMOND: Nearly as bad
as the Aston Martin Vanquish crashing.

54
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,925
照这么开下去，总有一天
他得把自己给弄死，
One of these days,
he's going to kill himself,

55
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:56,000
到时候咱就得换个新斯提格了。
（第三季第一集伏笔）
we are going to need a new Stig.
(Foreshadowing for S03E01)

56
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,600
一个替补斯提格。
- 没错。
A replacement Stig.
- Yeah.

57
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,640
不过言归正传，撞车撇开不谈，
这确实是一台奇快无比的车。
圈速摆在这儿，证据确凿。
Nevertheless, crash aside,
it is a very, very fast car.
There's the time, to prove it.

58
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,960
所以冲着这点，
我觉得他们就应该
把它引进到咱们国家来。
So on the strength of that,
I think they should
bring it into this country.

59
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
所以我真心觉得他们应该弄到这儿来卖。
So I think they should bring it over here.

60
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,800
在英国开卖？
哈蒙德：对啊。
Sell it in Britain?
HAMMOND: Yeah.

61
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,440
但实际上，这并不是
我们今晚要聊的话题。
Actually that's not what
we're talking about tonight.

62
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:08,760
今晚我们根本不在乎车跑得有多快，
We don't care how fast cars go tonight,

63
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,200
也不在乎它们长什么样。
we don't care what they look like.

64
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:13,600
我们在乎的是——
这车到底够不够酷。
What we care is whether
they're cool or not.

65
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:14,680
这么跟你们解释吧，
你们不妨这么想。
Let's try to explain, is,
think of it like this.

66
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,720
这有点像时尚改造节目《What Not To Wear》。
It's a bit like What Not To Wear.

67
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:19,320
你是特里妮，而我就是苏珊娜。
You are Trinny, and I am Susannah.

68
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,320
这画面可真得靠点想象力了。
[现场观众大笑]
Takes some imagining, that.
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

69
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,720
你们笑什么笑？
Why are you laughing?

70
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:25,120
我简直就跟苏珊娜·康斯坦丁一模一样好吗。
I am exactly like Susannah Constantine.

71
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:28,280
大街上成天有人
把我错认成她。
People are always mistaking me
for her in the streets.

72
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,520
怪让人尴尬的。
Embarrassing.

73
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,440
问题是，我觉得特里妮和苏珊娜
肯定不会有多待见这台NSX。
The thing is, I don't think Trinny and
Susannah would much care for the NSX.

74
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,560
它确实技术登峰造极，
It's very, very clever,

75
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,440
但它就像你给家里的高保真音响
买的那种死贵死贵的功放，
but it's like one of those expensive
amplifiers you buy for your hi-fi,

76
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,080
聪明绝顶，但透着一股理工宅男味。
clever, but a bit nerdy.

77
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,640
瞧瞧这个。这才算得上是
特里妮和苏珊娜会开的车。
Now, this. This is much more
a Trinny and Susannah car.

78
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:45,360
这是全新的雷诺Vel Satis，
It's the new Renault Vel Satis,

79
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,320
长相极其诡异的一坨玩意儿，
a completely weird-looking thing,

80
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:51,080
这是任谁也洗不掉的事实，
尤其是它那个大屁股。
no getting away from that,
especially round at the back.

81
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:55,480
但在那——我不得不说
还挺酷炫的外壳之下，
But beneath the, I have to say
quite cool exterior,

82
00:03:55,520 --> 00:04:00,200
它其实是一台对标宝马5系的五座轿车。
it's a five-seater rival
for the BMW 5 Series.

83
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,760
2.0升版本起售价大约两万英镑。
Prices start around £20,000
for the two-litre version.

84
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:06,520
这是一台给商务精英开的车，
It's a car for businessmen,

85
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,280
所以我觉得，最好的测试方法，
so, I thought
it would be a good idea

86
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:11,160
就是把它开到商务连锁酒店的大本营，
to take it to the epicentre
of the executive hotel

87
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:16,720
开到那个盛产免熨商务西裤的地方——斯温登。
in the crease-free business
lifestyle trouser, Swindon.

88
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:21,640
这里就是著名的M4走廊。
This is the M4 corridor.

89
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:27,360
遍地都是商务精英，一本正经地操持着他们的商务买卖。
Lots of businessmen here going about
their business in a businesslike fashion.

90
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,200
瞧瞧这位！再看那个！
Look at him! Look at that!

91
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:34,440
正火急火燎赶去二极管系统公司开商务会议呢。
Rushing off to a business meeting
at Diodine Systems.

92
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:39,720
去跟“亏死你点康”网站的哥们儿聊聊他的“后端”业务。
Talk about his back end
with a chap from losealotofmoney.com.

93
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:41,760
妙极了。
Marvellous.

94
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:54,000
无论商务人士在跑高速时
想从座驾里得到什么，
Whatever the businessman wants
from his car while he is driving
down the motorway,

95
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:56,640
他都能在这台 Vel Satis 上找到。
he's going to find it in the Vel Satis.

96
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,320
它非常安静、非常舒服、非常扎实，
It's very quiet,
very comfortable, very solid

97
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:01,320
而且车里放眼望去全都是木头，
and with all this wood everywhere,

98
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,920
开着它简直就像坐在古董专家亚瑟·内格斯的家具里一样。
it's like driving along in Arthur Negus.

99
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,480
动力也毫不逊色。在快车道上，
它完全能跟各路豪强一较高下。
There's power too. In the outside lane,
it'll dance with the best of them.

100
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:17,760
眼前这台搭载3.5升V6发动机的版本，
极速能飙到每小时147英里。
This version with the 3.5-litre V6
will do 147 miles an hour.

101
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,640
好了，我们到了。
And here we are.

102
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:26,760
15号出口，通往斯温登的大门。
Turn-off 15, the gateway to Swindon.

103
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:31,200
然而，哎呀糟糕，一到普通路面上，
And, oh, dear, on normal roads,

104
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:34,480
这种软绵绵的悬挂就让整台车开始崩盘了。
the soft ride means everything starts
to fall apart.

105
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,080
嗯……
Mmm.

106
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:40,840
照这么开上几英里，我非得睡死过去不可。
A few miles of this and I'd be fast asleep.

107
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,680
不过根本睡不成，
Except I wouldn't be,

108
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:49,080
因为每当车轮压过一个坑洼、
或者一颗反光道钉、
because every time it runs over a pothole
or a cat's eye

109
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,680
又或者是路面上随便什么坑槽，
or a groove in the road of some kind,

110
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:54,520
就会传来一声巨响，外加一阵剧烈的震颤。
there's an almighty crash and a shudder.

111
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,560
然后你就会被惊醒。
And you wake up.

112
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,520
真是烦死人了。
It's very annoying.

113
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,560
它确实跑得快，
It's capable of going fast

114
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:08,520
正如维多利亚女王确实也能跑步一样——
in the same way that Queen Victoria
was capable of running,

115
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:11,960
只是它打心底里根本不乐意罢了。
it just doesn't seem to like it very much.

116
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,720
所以，要是你赶着去开商务会议快迟到了，
So, if you're late for a business meeting,

117
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,400
你还不如踩个弹跳高跷去呢。
you're better off using a pogo stick.

118
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,280
或者手脚并用爬过去。
Or going on your hands and knees.

119
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:24,320
这台 Vel Satis 就像一颗牛油果，
表皮古怪，大部分果肉软趴趴，
The Vel Satis is like an avocado,
funny skin and mostly soft,

120
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:27,880
正中间却出人意料地藏着一颗坚硬如铁的果核。
but with a surprising
rock-hard stone in the middle.

121
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:32,400
这么说吧，单论车本身，它真不咋地。
As a car then, it isn't very good.

122
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:34,440
但它的外观造型
But will the styling

123
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:38,400
能否在这帮“西装男野生动物园”里
给它拉回一点颜面呢？
compensate for that here
at a safari park for the men in suits?

124
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,360
也就是斯温顿商务园区。
A Swindon business park.

125
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,560
我虽然还没来得及好好转转，
I haven't had chance to explore yet,

126
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:50,240
但我闭着眼睛都知道这里会有什么，
but I know exactly what's going to be here,

127
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:53,040
因为全天下的商务园区
全都一个德行。
because it will be the same
as every other business park.

128
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,800
到处都是黑黢黢的茶色大玻璃，
There'll be a lot of smoked glass,

129
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:57,920
所有的树都只有四英尺高，
all the trees will be four feet high

130
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,920
因为树龄跟这片大楼同岁。
because they're the same age
as the buildings.

131
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,600
至于那些绿植嘛，
只存在于商务园区里，
The plants, well, they exist
only in business parks,

132
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,920
你在任何植物学教材里都休想找着……
you won't find them in any textbook...

133
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:08,000
呃，还会有一个假装自己是人工湖的小水坑。
Er, there'll be a puddle
masquerading as a lake.

134
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:10,840
正当中肯定立着个所谓的“核心地标建筑”，
There'll be a sort of
central structure in the middle,

135
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,960
搞个视觉中心，假装很有“社区归属感”。
a focal point to give a sense of community.

136
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,040
嗯……还有啥来着？
Erm... what else?

137
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,160
减速带。
Speed bumps.

138
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,480
成百上千个。
Hundreds.

139
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,960
多到令人发指的减速带。
Hundreds and hundreds of speed bumps.

140
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:21,920
铺天盖地，哪儿哪儿都是。
They'll be everywhere.

141
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:28,720
又是茶色玻璃，还是茶色玻璃。
More smoked glass, more smoked glass.

142
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:31,120
还有……噢，减速带这就来了。
More... oh, there's a speed bump.

143
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:34,600
瞅瞅这植物，连蒂奇马什看了都得抓瞎。
Here's a plant that would stump Titchmarsh.

144
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:37,720
他绝对认不出这是个什么玩意儿。
完全两眼一抹黑。
He'd have no idea what that was.
None at all.

145
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:43,880
还有个巴掌大的小水洼，
我敢打赌他们管这叫“湖”。
And there's a very small puddle
which I bet they call the lake.

146
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:49,400
现在，就差找到那个核心标志物了，
Now, all we need to find now
is the central structure,

147
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:53,280
那个能让我产生“归属感”的东西。
something to give me
a sense of belonging here.

148
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,840
噢，减速带！
Oh, speed bump!

149
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:59,120
不对，看那边，居然是一座风车！
No, look, it's there, it's a windmill!

150
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,240
减速带。
Speed bump.

151
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,760
一座风车！
A windmill!

152
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:05,400
真是见鬼了，谁能想到这儿会立个风车？
Well, whoever would have
thought it would be there?

153
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:08,360
挺好的，真是有品味极了。
That's nice, that's very nice.

154
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:16,240
这车被这堆减速带彻底教做人了。
This car is completely stumped
by speed bumps.

155
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:18,840
滤震质感简直让人绝望。
It has a truly hopeless ride.

156
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:22,000
但这还不是它最大的硬伤。
But that is not its biggest problem.

157
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,760
眼前这整套环境才是。
All this is.

158
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:27,280
这才是商务精英们梦寐以求的：
随大流，千篇一律。
This is what the businessman wants,
conformity.

159
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,120
一台饮水机，
A water fountain,

160
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:32,440
一个叫珍妮特的平庸女秘书，
